        <div class="col-sm-8 main-content">
            <article id="MainContentPlaceholder_T225F410C003_Col00" class="sf_colsIn" data-placeholder-label="Main Content">
    
    <h1>Irish Retail Payments Forum</h1><p>The Irish Retail Payments Forum (IRPF) has been established by the Central Bank of Ireland&nbsp;in order to provide a forum in which payment services providers (PSPs) and payment services users (PSUs) can come together to engage in an open and constructive dialogue with each other in relation to Irish retail payment services generally.</p><p>The principal aims of the IRPF are:</p><div class="regulationContent"><ol><li>to promote the continued safety and efficiency of retail payments in Ireland and; </li><li>to foster co-operation between all stakeholders in relation to the development and provision of new and improved payment services
    and payment instruments. </li></ol></div><p>For more information, you can view the&nbsp;<a title="Irish Retail Payments Forum Terms of Reference" href="/docs/default-source/financial-system/irish-retail-payments-forum/irish-retail-payments-forum-terms-of-reference.pdf?sfvrsn=74949e1d_2">Irish Retail Payments Forum Terms of Reference (PDF 427.61KB)</a>.</p><p>If you require any further information please contact the Payment Systems Policy team in the Bank at &nbsp;<a href="mailto:paymentsystemspolicy@centralbank.ie">paymentsystemspolicy@centralbank.ie</a>.</p>
    
   





<div class="panel panel-default standard-accordion">
    <div class="panel-heading" id="heading-IRPF-Members-df3d941b-0bd6-49b4-875b-fcdc3bb9bfe7">
        <div class="panel-title">
            <a class="collapsed gtm-expanding" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" href="#IRPF-Members-df3d941b-0bd6-49b4-875b-fcdc3bb9bfe7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="IRPF-Members-df3d941b-0bd6-49b4-875b-fcdc3bb9bfe7">
                <strong class="gtm-expanding">IRPF Members</strong>

            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div id="IRPF-Members-df3d941b-0bd6-49b4-875b-fcdc3bb9bfe7" class="panel-collapse collapse " aria-labelledby="heading-IRPF-Members-df3d941b-0bd6-49b4-875b-fcdc3bb9bfe7">
        <div class="panel-body">
            <p>The IRPF currently consists of the following institutions and representative bodies:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Banking &amp; Payments Federation Ireland (BPFI)</li>
    <li>Central Bank of Ireland</li>
    <li>Competition and Consumer Protection Commission (CCPC)</li>
    <li>Consumers&rsquo; Association of Ireland</li>
    <li>Convenience Stores and Newsagents Association (CSNA)</li>
    <li>Credit Union Compliance Centre</li>
    <li>Credit Union Development Association (CUDA)</li>
    <li>Department of Employment Affairs and Social Protection</li>
    <li>Department of Finance</li>
    <li>E-Commerce Association of Ireland</li>
    <li>Electronic Money Association</li>
    <li>Fintech &amp; Payments Association of Ireland (FPAI)</li>
    <li>Irish League of Credit Unions (ILCU)</li>
    <li>Irish Payments Council</li>
    <li>Irish Small and Medium Enterprises Association (ISME)</li>
    <li>MasterCard</li>
    <li>National Transport Authority (NTA)</li>
    <li>Retail Excellence</li>
    <li>Retail Grocery, Dairy &amp; Allied Trades Association (RGDATA)</li>
    <li>Retail Ireland (IBEC)</li>
    <li>Rotational Credit Institution (currently Bank of Ireland)</li>
    <li>Rotational E-Money Institution (currently Remitly Europe Ltd)</li>
    <li>Rotational Payment Institution (currently Stripe)</li>
    <li>VISA</li>
</ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>





<div class="panel panel-default standard-accordion">
    <div class="panel-heading" id="heading-Euro-Retail-Payments-Board-8ce481c2-5847-49fc-9923-64644bed9a2a">
        <div class="panel-title">
            <a class="collapsed gtm-expanding" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" href="#Euro-Retail-Payments-Board-8ce481c2-5847-49fc-9923-64644bed9a2a" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="Euro-Retail-Payments-Board-8ce481c2-5847-49fc-9923-64644bed9a2a">
                <strong class="gtm-expanding">Euro Retail Payments Board</strong>

            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div id="Euro-Retail-Payments-Board-8ce481c2-5847-49fc-9923-64644bed9a2a" class="panel-collapse collapse " aria-labelledby="heading-Euro-Retail-Payments-Board-8ce481c2-5847-49fc-9923-64644bed9a2a">
        <div class="panel-body">
            <p>The objective of the Euro Retail Payments&nbsp;Board (ERPB) is to contribute to and to facilitate the further development of an integrated, innovative and competitive market for euro retail payments in the EU by:</p><ul><li>identifying and studying technical, behavioural and legal obstacles in &ndash; but not limited to - credit transfer payments, direct debit payments, card payments, internet payments, mobile payments and payments-related horizontal issues (e.g. issues
        related to standards, fraud and security);</li><li>identifying and pursuing ways to address these obstacles; and</li><li>identifying and pursuing ways to foster innovation, competition and integration in retail payments in euro in the EU.</li></ul><p>For more information, you can visit the&nbsp;<a target="_blank" href="https://www.ecb.europa.eu/paym/retpaym/euro/html/index.en.html">ERPB website</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

    
    <p><strong>See also:</strong></p><ul><li><a href="/financial-system/payments-and-securities-settlements/irish-retail-payments-forum/summary-meetings-notes">Summary Meeting Notes</a></li><li><a href="/financial-system/payments-and-securities-settlements/irish-retail-payments-forum/paybac-wg">Pay by Account (PAYBAC) Working Group</a></li></ul>
    
   

            
            </article>
        </div>
